# g96-be-memory-channels: what the lead applies (hot files only)

## 1. native/core/Cargo.toml  [workspace.dependencies]
Add, in alphabetical place (next to `url`/`uuid`):
    webpki-roots = "1.0.11"
Cargo.lock: in the `[[package]] name = "mixdog-mcp"` entry add `"webpki-roots",` to its dependencies (the crate is already in the
lock at 1.0.11 as a transitive dependency of reqwest, so nothing new is fetched). mixdog-mcp/Cargo.toml already carries
`webpki-roots = { workspace = true }` (my file). If the hakari workspace-hack needs a refresh for it, regenerate it.
Used by: mixdog-mcp/src/gmail_verify/mod.rs GmailAppPassword::new (Mozilla's bundled roots next to the system roots, as Node's list).

## 2. native/core/crates/mixdog-app-server-daemon/src/compose_flip.rs
Anchor: the line `let scheduler = mixdog_services::scheduler::Scheduler::new(schedule_store.clone(), ...` (about line 1313).
Add directly after it:
    scheduler.set_prompts_dir(b.data_dir.join("prompts"), b.tokens.durability_io); // schedule.prompt (or `<name>.md` when empty) names a file under <DATA_DIR>/prompts, or an absolute path; read on the durability lane
Without it no prompt file is read (inline text still works).

## 3. SERVICE_PENDING (compose_flip.rs)
Nothing to remove: this task registers no service and adds no protocol method.

